# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Text is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF on every platform, Windows included.
#
# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half. A bare `text=auto` would normalise only what is stored, and a
# Windows checkout would still be handed CRLF — where a bash script whose shebang line ends in a
# carriage return fails with an error that names neither the file nor the cause, and a parser that
# splits on a bare newline reads every value as absent rather than crashing.
#
# It is stated once for every path rather than per extension so that it still holds for the next
# script somebody adds, whatever it is named or wherever it lives. Nothing tracked here needs CRLF
# in the working tree: there are no Windows batch or PowerShell scripts in this repository.
#
# packages/core/spec/lineEndingPolicy.spec.ts pins the result for every file carrying a shebang.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary content, marked so that no conversion or diff heuristic can reach it. These are
# the binary types actually tracked here; `text=auto` above still detects anything else.
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
